"""Offline workflow help shared by Connection and About."""

from PySide6.QtWidgets import QComboBox, QDialog, QDialogButtonBox, QTextBrowser, QVBoxLayout

from bnkg.ui.components import CONNECTION_HELP

TOPICS = {
    "Connection and diagnostics": CONNECTION_HELP
    + "\n\nConnection evidence\nConnection shows the last verified identity, firmware when supplied, sample freshness and advertised supported controls. Disconnected/stale evidence is labelled, not treated as live. An HTTP response or mDNS advertisement is only a candidate until the Web-XI SLM handshake succeeds. A denied request does not by itself prove a missing licence. No automatic scans, retries of writes or reconnection occur.\n\nCopy support summary collects only local runtime/state/count information by default. Device identity/address is an explicit option. Passwords, raw readings, local report notes and arbitrary error text are excluded. Review the copied summary before sharing; nothing is uploaded automatically.",
    "Measurement meanings": "Instrument values first\nDashboard/Frequency use direct SLM values. Missing A/C/Z data stays unavailable. Current LAF/LZF are time-weighted levels. Whole-measurement LAeq/LZeq are cumulative equivalent levels. A verified interval Leq needs its own documented integration period. Fast weighting or a 250 ms output period does not establish 125 ms Leq.\n\nCalculated values must be labelled with their basis. Demo values remain synthetic and isolated. Live/Frozen/Saved identifies source, not the averaging period. Only compare compatible axes/scopes. Cross-check displayed information on the meter; this software does not certify measurement or regulatory compliance.",
    "Saved sessions and export": "Capture, logging and saved data\nLocal capture keeps a bounded view. File logging preserves all recorded samples. Clear view only never deletes logs. Browse history opens BnKG SQLite sessions read-only, 100 rows per page; Chart this page plots that page, not the full session. Saved Frequency uses the selected row's retained descriptors, not live setup. Unsupported BKC analysis remains unavailable. Device file downloads preserve originals and do not invoke instrument Open.\n\nExports run independently from a consistent snapshot while monitoring/logging continue. Choose another session only after stopping local logging. CSV/TSV/TXT are scalar tables; JSON/NDJSON/XLSX/HTML can include richer metadata and direct spectra. Local report details appear only in metadata-bearing formats. Cancellation removes owned partial outputs; XLSX packaging may finish first. HTML is a basic report; PDF/DOCX are later work.",
    "Export presets and contents": "Export options\nThe preview describes requested output without scanning the source. Scalar text formats omit session metadata/formulas, events and spectra. JSON/NDJSON, XLSX and HTML retain metadata and parameter details; XLSX alone contains the Events sheet. Raw JSON/NDJSON payloads and requested spectral context can contain unselected readings and private metadata. Turning off raw is not anonymization. Local review markers and Exclude labels are not merged or applied.\n\nShow export presets offers built-in and named local profiles. Choosing previews; Apply changes options; Export remains separate. Up to 20 unique names of 60 characters are stored locally with format, scalar IDs and raw/spectrum flags only. Presets never auto-apply or contain paths/measurements. At least one scalar is required. Options lock during export and the running preview keeps its captured source/options even if logging changes session. Original logs and existing destinations are preserved.",
    "Parameter visibility and presets": "Dashboard visibility\nSearch IDs, descriptions, scopes and formulas; choose a group or Selected only. Filters preserve hidden checkboxes. Select shown/Clear shown affect matching selectable rows, with one-step bulk undo. Manual changes clear that undo. Calculated differences remain separate from direct instrument tiles.\n\nChoose a preset to preview it; Apply preset replaces the full Dashboard selection, including hidden rows. Save new preset stores the current selection locally under a unique name (up to 20 presets and 60 characters per name). Deleting a saved preset keeps the current selection. Unsupported stored presets are retained with editing disabled. Existing empty selections and visibility preferences remain valid. No preset enables an instrument output or changes acquisition, logging, chart selection, exports or SLM configuration.",
    "Local review markers": "Saved review\nRows and Chart this page share an exact sample-ID selection and a preview reconstructed from that row’s retained descriptors. Selected values has its own tab. Charts show at most 100 rows; duplicate timestamps overlap, so use Rows to disambiguate.\n\nM1/M2/M3/Exclude are local review labels. Set a range start and select its end on the same page, or mark a single row. Exclude does not remove data or recalculate Leq. Marker ribbons show recorded points, not continuous integration intervals.\n\nSave review as creates a separate new .bnkg-review.json snapshot. Keep the original SQLite log; a review contains only notes and verified references. Open review checks session identity and fingerprints of all marked rows. Existing files are not overwritten. Unsaved marker changes prompt before refresh, session change or exit, but drafts are not crash recovery backups. Limits: 128 markers, 100 rows per marker, 1,000 row references, 500 characters per note, 1 MB file and four-second verification. Review notes may be private and are not merged into ordinary exports.",
    "Display and recording": "Display tools\nFit (both dimensions)/100%/200%/400%, Pixel—Nearest Neighbor/Sharp—Lanczos/Smooth—Bicubic and fullscreen are local rendering choices. Original PNG saving retains incoming bytes; processed PNG saving re-encodes at display scale without the status overlay. Check freshness first. Arming persists for this connection through successful actions. Acknowledge a fresh measurement screen once for arrows without repeated dialogs. Menu / OK opens once and locks the keypad; return physically before acknowledging again. Menu editing, critical writes and automatic retries remain blocked.\n\nRecording\nExplicit screen recording retains original PNGs and a receipt/hash/gap ledger in a new folder. It continues across pages, independently of scalar capture. Stop finishes accepted frames; Cancel keeps originals. Optional external FFmpeg/ffprobe creates lossy AVC MP4 after capture, with held frames through gaps. Consult the timing sidecar. No external encoder executable is bundled and no automatic wake occurs. Audio/playback/export controls are available below, with their own limits. Existing one-second polling is unchanged; short live 2255 and external encoder checks passed; long-run and physical display sleep/wake remain unverified. MP4 options include download links, placement instructions and Browse controls. Caps are eight queued frames, one hour, 3,600 frames, 512 MiB PNGs and 512 MiB encoded output, with low-disk/no-frame stops.",
    "Metadata, local reports and location": "Three separate sources\nInstrument fields come from received SLM outputs/setup. Search and group filters affect display only; checked fields remain on the Dashboard. Access flags describe the device and do not authorize new application writes.\n\nLocal report details are user-entered project/operator/site/notes on this PC. Save local draft retains them for future logs; new logs take an immutable copy at logging start. Changing a draft never changes an old log or writes a device field. Optional project/site filenames are sanitized and retain a UTC timestamp.\n\nLocation / transfer contains a manual draft, initially a user-supplied default, not a GPS fix. Copying available SLM coordinates records their source and PC receipt time, not a verified fix timestamp. Map links are explicit and send coordinates to the external provider only when opened. The existing single enabled Text-slot transfer still needs preview, arming, two confirmations, idle-state checks, read-back and audit. It never changes native GPS. No bulk metadata writer or automatic PC/phone location acquisition is implemented.",
}


class WorkflowHelp(QDialog):
    def __init__(self, parent=None, topic="Connection and diagnostics"):
        super().__init__(parent)
        self.setWindowTitle("B&KG workflow help")
        self.resize(660, 640)
        layout = QVBoxLayout(self)
        self.topics = QComboBox()
        self.topics.addItems(TOPICS)
        layout.addWidget(self.topics)
        self.text = QTextBrowser()
        layout.addWidget(self.text)
        self.topics.currentTextChanged.connect(lambda name: self.text.setPlainText(TOPICS[name]))
        self.topics.setCurrentText(topic if topic in TOPICS else next(iter(TOPICS)))
        self.text.setPlainText(TOPICS[self.topics.currentText()])
        buttons = QDialogButtonBox(QDialogButtonBox.StandardButton.Close)
        buttons.rejected.connect(self.reject)
        layout.addWidget(buttons)
